  "authorization": "Owner explicitly requested intraday completed-sale recording and same-day replacement review on September 15, plus clear Exit wording. Repair preserves frozen selections and engine rules; actual fills reconcile into completed sessions. Strong ETag sync repair preserves conditional writes. See docs/research/c1-intraday-activity-20260915.md. Follow-up owner screenshot shows hidden trade entry. Surface the existing opening error and explicit read-only retry in Account settings; log opening failure for diagnosis. No recommendation gates are changed. Owner follow-up shows DELL price-basis mismatch blocking an already-completed STX exit. Add accounting-only recording of existing pending exits with canonical replay reconciliation; preserve all buy checks, and expose compared market-data values for diagnosis. See docs/research/c1-recorded-exit-independence-20260915.md. Owner requests repair of DELL 534.08/534.28 revision blocking purchases. Require repeat-consistent provider OHLC, no prior account exposure, and identical opening/current-price economic plans under both price bases. Preserve original inputs and all strategy checks; no price tolerance. See docs/research/c1-opening-price-review-20260915.md. Owner explicitly requests repair of occupied-slot recommendations after the recorded STX sale. Recheck failed current entry gates before projection, preserve actual sale economics and saved selection evidence through closing replay. Frozen ranking, opening quotes, sizing and risk parameters are unchanged. See docs/research/c1-intraday-slot-repair-20260915.md. Owner explicitly approved action-card wording changes on September 15: lead with Buy/Add share quantity, remove Manual and Review now, clarify reference prices and refresh time. Presentation only; see docs/research/c1-action-wording-20260915.md. Owner explicitly requests repair of the September 15 EOD update. Reconcile only the independently reviewed held DELL close/volume correction with exact economic parity and immutable history; evaluate private exposure at the prior revised date. See docs/research/c1-held-close-review-20260915.md. Only affected application hashes updated; guard and build hooks unchanged. Owner requests Fix all after the four-defect audit on September 16. Evidence-preserving archive recovery, repeat-confirmed economically identical held-model close corrections, NYSE early-close handling and retained intraday audit evidence; see docs/research/c1-operational-recovery-20260916.md. No strategy or actual account exposure guard changes. Owner requests repair of September 17 provider finalization failure: hash-bound archived evidence, exact model economics and independent private-account replay/plan parity. See docs/research/c1-september17-finalization.md. Only affected application hash entries change; release guard unchanged. Production follow-up recovers the exact reviewed contemporaneous September 17 capture before later provider adjustments; all connect and private-account parity checks remain enforced. Owner directs future verified FMP revisions to use append-only automatic reconciliation rather than date-specific code patches. Require independently repeated immutable evidence for every revised adjusted bar plus exact model and private-account replay parity; allow unrelated symbols to settle in different captures, preserve original history and all frozen C1 rules, and log only bounded reconciliation diagnostics. See docs/research/c1-automatic-provider-reconciliation-20260922.md. Owner reported a completed FCX sale and requested repair of the form that offered only stop orders. Add an accounting-only completed-sale path for owned shares, preserve exact broker facts through replay, reject discretionary purchases, and clarify prior-session saving. See docs/research/c1-owner-recorded-exit-20260922.md. Owner then showed that the calculated MPC replacement disappeared from the after-close selector. Recover only that completed-session queue from the accepted hash-bound opening and recorded owner exit; require the actual broker fill before persistence. See docs/research/c1-completed-owner-exit-recovery-20260922.md. Owner requested correction of the saved MPC execution time without duplicating the purchase. Permit timestamp-only correction of the original ticket and allocated fills with full replay, regular-session validation and unchanged economics. See docs/research/c1-intraday-time-correction-20260922.md. Owner showed a C1 account read timeout that exposed account activation despite an intact saved account. Align the client timeout with the endpoint budget, retain state through transient failures and require an authoritative 404 before activation. See docs/research/c1-timeout-state-retention-20260923.md. Owner then showed the only saved transaction was the FCX sale with an incorrect price and no MPC ticket. Permit correction of price, fee and time on the existing ticket while locking identity, symbol, side, shares and allocation; replay exact cash economics and sync the corrected decision. See docs/research/c1-intraday-detail-correction-20260923.md. Owner then showed DELL price-history reconciliation blocking the entire account after repeated FMP changes. Accept each independently repeat-confirmed symbol, defer only unstable rows on their prior accepted bars, preserve exact model economics, and keep the actual private account on its recorded basis instead of requiring a hypothetical alternate-history plan. See docs/research/c1-operational-provider-reconciliation-20260923.md.",
